    {
      "id": 164908,
      "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
      "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-07T00:14:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ironic\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/48/2171_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ironic:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's fair.&nbsp;My frustration on things like the Akash stuff isn't so much the belief that all the Playtesters are in on some big secret, it's that it seems to me that sometimes, you guys forget you're in the portion of the forums where a lot of people aren't testers at all, so you make these seemingly all-inclusive statements which don't apply to the full conversation - such as this thread, where two people mentioned the Tactics Akash without specifying that it was currently just in testing.The link is much more helpful - thanks for posting it!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think that you're missatributing the problem. &nbsp;While I've seen the sort of thing that you describe happen, it's almost always in regards to information gained from twitch chats, livestreams, obscure forum posts, kickstarter comments, tweets, card art, Tactics scenarios and occasionally reported live conversations, and pretty much never from playtester threads. &nbsp;It's all information that's publicly available, but often hard to find. &nbsp;(Although card art and Tactics stuff is unavailable if you don't have the product).</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:46:12.170Z",
