    {
      "id": 164909,
      "name": "Ironic",
      "username": "Ironic",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-03-07T00:23:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Perhaps I should be more general, then.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think it's best if people on the message boards say where any piece of information originates, rather than assuming that we're all spending hours a week keep up with the Twitch stream and so forth.&nbsp; Name-checking Akash'Bhuta, which can be found on the GTG site or the wiki is not and will never be analogous to name-checking Akash'Dharsha, for which a Google search will yield the Facebook page of person who doesn't even have that exact name.&nbsp; Regardless of where it originates, the barrier there is a real one.</p>",
